by the separate license in the folder above.

2. OWNERSHIP
Word Cue is owned by Bryson Woods, Fresh Fire Studios. Being able to see the
source code does not make it open source.

3. WHAT YOU MAY DO
- Download official releases of Word Cue from Fresh Fire Studios and use
  them free of charge, in any church, ministry, or personal setting, on as
  many Macs as you like.
- Read the source code to understand how Word Cue works or to check that it
  keeps its privacy promises.
- Build the source code on your own Mac only to examine or test it.
- Report problems and suggest changes. Suggestions you send may be used in
  Word Cue without payment or credit.

4. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION
- Copy, modify, or redistribute the source code or any build made from it.
- Publish, share, or sell your own builds of Word Cue or Word Cue Lab.
- Use any part of the code, rules, data files, or designs in another app,
  product, or service.
- Charge for Word Cue, or bundle it with something you charge for.
- Remove or change copyright notices.

